# VitePress build/cache
docs/.vitepress/cache
# Fixture tree written by the CLI e2e test. It lives inside the package so the schema it
# writes can resolve drizzle-orm by the normal node_modules walk.
packages/*/test/.e2e-tmp
packages/*/test/.cmd-tmp
# One pattern rather than a name per test file. This was an enumerated list, and it worked right
# up until a new spec picked a directory nobody had added to it: 22 generated modules landed in a
# merged commit, carrying a pid in the filename so they could never even be overwritten.
packages/*/test/.tmp-*

# Agent worktrees. Claude Code creates isolated checkouts here for parallel work.
.claude/worktrees/

# Scratch copies of a script, left in place when a run is interrupted. A killed reviewer left three
# 440KB copies of verify-packed.sh sitting in scripts/, none of them ignored and all of them
# committable. Same failure as the enumerated test-tmp list above: the leak lands where nobody
# thought to look, so match a shape rather than a name.
scripts/*-rr[0-9]*.sh
scripts/*.tmp.sh
scripts/vp-*.sh
